 35CL c  1969Ha17: 51-61-MeV {+35}Cl{+5,6+} beams of 80 nA were produced from   
 35CL2c  the Chalk River MP tandem accelerator and bombarded 9.6-mg/cm{+2}      
 35CL3c  carbon and 5-mg/cm{+2} {+24}Mg. De-excitation |g rays were detected    
 35CL4c  using two 40-cm{+3} Ge(Li) detectors at 125|' and at 0|' or 90|'.      
 35CL5c  Measured E|g, I|g(|q). Deduced levels, mixing ratio, transition        
 35CL6c  strengths, T{-1/2} for 2 levels using the Doppler Shift Attenuation    
 35CL7c  Method (DSAM).                                                         
 35CL c  1977Sc36: 53-56-MeV {+35}Cl{+6+} beams of 60 nA were produced from a   
 35CL2c  single MP Tandem Van de Graaff tandem accelerator at the three-stage   
 35CL3c  facility of Brookhaven National Laboratory. Targets were 23Na and 27Al.
 35CL4c  De-excitation |g rays were detected using a 55- cm{+3} coaxial Ge(Li)  
 35CL5c  detector at 0|'. Measured E|g, I|g(|q). Deduced levels, mixing ratios, 
 35CL6c  transition strengths, T{-1/2} for the levels of 1220, 1762 and 2650 keV
 35CL7c  using the Doppler Shift Attenuation Method (DSAM).                     
